# Examples where .gitignore should remain empty:
# If only source files like .js, .css, .py, .java, .go, .cpp, .h, .md, .txt, .json, .yml, .yaml, .toml, .cfg, .ini are in the changes
# and there are no build artifacts, dependencies, or temporary files, then output nothing.

# In this case, the changes are only JavaScript and CSS source files:
# scripts/audio.js, scripts/endings.js, scripts/main.js, scripts/ui.js, styles/main.css
# No build artifacts, dependencies, or temp files detected.

# Therefore, no .gitignore rules are needed for these changes.